  card: `Aegon, the king's eldest son by his second queen, is crowned in the Dragonpit by Ser Criston Cole. The master of coin, Lyman Beesbury, spoke for Rhaenyra in council and did not leave it alive; the accounts of how he died disagree. A Kingsguard knight, Steffon Darklyn, carries the old king's crown to Dragonstone and Rhaenyra is crowned with it. Two courts, two councils, a Kingsguard and a Queensguard. Aegon's terms are refused. Rhaenyra's council counts twelve fighting dragons on Dragonstone to the greens' four, but only five riders fit to fly them. Then the dragons go: Aemond to buy Storm's End with a betrothal, Daemon to take Harrenhal, Jacaerys north to the Vale, White Harbor and Winterfell.`,
