  card: `Widowed at Rook's Rest, Corlys Velaryon threatens to leave; Jacaerys, back from the north, keeps him by making him Hand of the Queen. The blacks have more dragons than riders, so Jacaerys offers a knighthood to anyone who can mount a riderless one. Many die trying, Ser Steffon Darklyn among them. Four succeed: Hugh Hammer on Vermithor, Ulf the White on Silverwing, Addam of Hull on Seasmoke and a girl called Nettles on Sheepstealer. Rhaenyra's two youngest sail for Pentos and meet ninety Triarchy warships in the Gullet: Stormcloud carries Aegon home and dies of his wounds, and Viserys is taken. Jacaerys and the new riders break the fleet, but Vermax flies too low and Jacaerys dies in the water.`,
