  fire: [{ d: 'caraxes', t0: 0.66, t1: 0.7 }, { d: 'vhagar', t0: 0.67, t1: 0.71 }],
  caps: [[0.05, "Rhaenyra, believing Nettles is Daemon's lover, orders Lord Mooton to send her the girl's head."], [0.12, "Mooton's maester warns Daemon. Nettles leaves on Sheepstealer and is never seen at court again."], [0.3, "Daemon flies to Harrenhal. Maidenpool raises Aegon's banners behind him."], [0.44, 'He waits thirteen days.'], [0.58, 'On the fourteenth, Aemond comes on Vhagar.'], [0.66, 'They fight above the Gods Eye. Caraxes was about half her size.'], [0.75, "Locked together, they fall. The tales say Daemon leapt onto Vhagar and drove his sword through Aemond's eye."], [0.84, "Caraxes drags himself ashore and dies beneath Harrenhal's walls. Daemon's body is never found."]],
  card: `Rhaenyra, believing Nettles has become Daemon's lover, orders Lord Mooton of Maidenpool to send her the girl's head. Mooton's maester warns Daemon instead. Nettles flies off on Sheepstealer over the Bay of Crabs and is never seen at court again; Mooton raises Aegon's banners the moment Daemon leaves. Daemon flies to Harrenhal and waits thirteen days. On the fourteenth, Aemond comes on Vhagar. They fight above the Gods Eye and fall into it locked together; the tales say Daemon leapt onto Vhagar's back and drove his sword through Aemond's blind eye. Vhagar dies in the lake. Caraxes drags himself ashore and dies beneath Harrenhal's walls. Daemon's body is never found.`,
  reading: 'The two largest assets destroy each other.',
